chapter_2_91345bff		He didn’t know what happened from then on. Had he fallen? He limply walked towards a wall to rest. All he could remember was he had promised Nabisin would be protected. No matter what.	game/chapter-2.rpy	28	"[what]"
chapter_2_17904ce9		The day came, and with it, the early morning sounds of birds chirping and the nearby market slowly woke Nabisin up. Nabisin felt so alone; the side of the bed previously occupied by Lulu was cold and lacked his figure.	game/chapter-2.rpy	31	"[what]"
chapter_2_4cb429bc		Still sluggish from the restless night, Nabisin realized the guards might have come for Lulu instead of him.	game/chapter-2.rpy	32	"[what]"
chapter_2_f9a1fa3c		Panting and still half-dressed, he hopped out of bed quickly and started to leave.	game/chapter-2.rpy	33	"[what]"
chapter_2_db687882		He suddenly heard heavy footsteps coming. The door had been left ajar all night as if someone had fled the house.	game/chapter-2.rpy	34	"[what]"
chapter_2_78b966d1		Lulu! No, he wouldn’t do that!	game/chapter-2.rpy	35	"[what]"
chapter_2_db09aab8		Nabisin pondered to himself. He was still unsure why he was alone and if that was the only explanation for why their house had been intact but devoid of Lulu.	game/chapter-2.rpy	36	"[what]"
chapter_2_0238e568	g	“Nabisin of the temple, come down immediately!”	game/chapter-2.rpy	39	g "[what]"
chapter_2_53cad73d		The guards’ voices hit like a hammer. Nabisin, completely frightened of what would happen, stood still, staring at the window, thinking of whether he should do something crazy.	game/chapter-2.rpy	40	"[what]"
chapter_2_4cfdb0dc		Instead, he complied with the orders, as any more offense to the guards other than making them wait meant costly fees, or far worse, death. They waited for Nabisin to appear.	game/chapter-2.rpy	41	"[what]"
chapter_2_b30033f9		Their faces were stoic, distant, and demanding authority, and by the time Nabisin was close enough, they pulled him by his arms and dragged him to the outside.	game/chapter-2.rpy	42	"[what]"
chapter_2_a9984dd9		The sunlight hit Nabisin in the eyes, temporarily blurring his vision. However, once everything started making sense again, some folks looked down on him some expecting this to happen, others worried about Nabisin’s fate from now on.	game/chapter-2.rpy	43	"[what]"
chapter_2_bb009b4e		The day’s heat struck him. A damp sensation soaked some of his garments, and the heavy cuffs made his wrists ache. The heavy bronze was abrasive, wounding Nabisin’s fragile flesh. 	game/chapter-2.rpy	44	"[what]"
chapter_2_d2688f1c		Everyone’s eyes were sharp upon him, as if hundreds of thorns were penetrating his skin while trudging through an unkempt garden. Occasionally their gazes averted back to their own business.	game/chapter-2.rpy	45	"[what]"
chapter_2_99482a71		Not long after, children that Nabisin recognized and some he even used to play with disappeared into the safety of the walls of their homes.	game/chapter-2.rpy	47	"[what]"
chapter_2_22003e5a		It was uncommon for someone to be imprisoned so early in the morning, as a priest’s daily duties were to give offerings to the gods. Space and time melded together.	game/chapter-2.rpy	48	"[what]"
chapter_2_733a4273		The palace’s streets, arches, and patios became a hot mess to Nabisin. All he could think about was Lulu and what could have become of him.	game/chapter-2.rpy	50	"[what]"
chapter_2_47e43927		Attempts to free himself from the guards’ tight hold proved futile. The path that was once familiar to Nabisin became the very reason why he wanted to stray away from it. He yearned to go back home, and clung to fleeting hope that the gods had spared Lulu.	game/chapter-2.rpy	51	"[what]"
chapter_2_ce617998		…	game/chapter-2.rpy	52	"[what]"
