chapter_2_ae6fb59c		Instead, it slipped from his hands, and the statuette, as if it had sprung to life, bounced upon the floor, rolling across the room until it stood upright.	game/chapter-2.rpy	250	"[what]"
chapter_2_53d4cbeb		Nabisin tried to grab the fleeting gift, jumping and spinning, which seemed to have a desire of its own, but once he caught the statuette, it refused to move from its spot, almost as if it was designed to be there.	game/chapter-2.rpy	251	"[what]"
chapter_2_01511f96		No matter how much force he applied to pull, twist, even knock the statuette over, it was melded to the ground.	game/chapter-2.rpy	252	"[what]"
chapter_2_72468685	g	“Hey, you there! Get off the ground, mutt. The scribes are already here.”	game/chapter-2.rpy	254	g "[what]"
chapter_2_2937eb47		Trying not to embarrass himself more, he rose from the ground and went back to his place. {w}He remembered when Shelibuum gave him the statuette and how, even though it had been less than a day, he had given the object emotional significance as a gift, hope, and love.	game/chapter-2.rpy	255	"[what]"
chapter_2_83a825e1		Yet it slipped from his hands as if it were forcibly jerked away, leading him to believe some otherworldly force animated it.	game/chapter-2.rpy	256	"[what]"
chapter_2_be01f317		He couldn’t understand the meaning of anything that happened within the last days or so.	game/chapter-2.rpy	257	"[what]"
chapter_2_1754591c		Remembering long lost memories that both reminded him of happier times of ignorance and the burning sensation that felt as if his skin was being torn apart, yet no signs of cuts. {w}Now add to the list his gift creating a mind of his own and attaching itself to the floor.	game/chapter-2.rpy	258	"[what]"
chapter_2_d5c76ac0		There was no explanation whatsoever. Being alone again was a mind-numbing experience. {w}He hadn’t been like this for years.	game/chapter-2.rpy	259	"[what]"
chapter_2_684b710d		He was always by Luludân, and yet right now, he felt as if the world had become a husk of itself. {w}He barely knew what was to come.	game/chapter-2.rpy	260	"[what]"
chapter_2_78434540		Suddenly, the room grew wider and taller. {w}Nabisin, at the center, stood still when he saw another familiar muzzle—that of Shelibuum, calming his nerves. {w}At least she was smiling, but soon, she turned her gaze back to her doings.	game/chapter-2.rpy	261	"[what]"
chapter_2_eed7670d	"Judge"	“Nabisin, The one who calls upon Sîn, may you be judged with the god’s favor on your side, and may the rivers spare you. We are united here for your offenses towards Utudug, he who is good, towards your unnatural liking for the same as your sex.”	game/chapter-2.rpy	263	"Judge" "[what]"
chapter_2_6ae47ce0	"Judge"	“Can you contest these accusations?”	game/chapter-2.rpy	264	"Judge" "[what]"
chapter_2_ef453d96		The piercing and demanding voice of the judge cut through the air. {w}Everyone, including Nabisin, was taken back to the memory of that night.	game/chapter-2.rpy	265	"[what]"
chapter_2_63c436e5		The offense was to speak up before a high member of the priests, their favorite in fact, and leave so soon as to displease the high priests who had traveled from far and wide.	game/chapter-2.rpy	266	"[what]"
chapter_2_bf8351dc		Nabisin tried to speak; {w}his mouth was gaping open several seconds before he could mutter any word under his breath.	game/chapter-2.rpy	267	"[what]"
chapter_2_fab79b24		Given his anger and almost desperation, he finally spurts some words.	game/chapter-2.rpy	268	"[what]"
chapter_2_96ea38e0	n	“It was not my intention to so disrespect and misbehave as my high rank so demands at the feast.”	game/chapter-2.rpy	270	n "[what]"
chapter_2_a387e7f3	n	“Utudug has always been a sore pain in my life. From the time we were paired during our training to this very sour day.”	game/chapter-2.rpy	271	n "[what]"
chapter_2_500af3e7		Trying to subdue his anger, he inhaled and exhaled in hopes of simmering down his hateful thoughts. {w}He calmly returned to his monologue.	game/chapter-2.rpy	272	"[what]"
chapter_2_ac63664c	n	“If thou hast a problem with what I do with my life, may the gods be in my favor and bring reason to this. {w}It is not your business to force yourself into my affairs and declare my desires to be inappropriate.”	game/chapter-2.rpy	273	n "[what]"
chapter_2_978e4b50	n	“Only the gods are to administrate these petty matters. {w}Haven’t you noticed the increasing danger of Euphrates flooding our fields? Of our foodstuffs decaying? It is known our instability has only begun.”	game/chapter-2.rpy	274	n "[what]"
chapter_2_aed950fd		The room fell into a deafening silence; even the judge and Utudug felt conflicted about speaking up again.	game/chapter-2.rpy	276	"[what]"
chapter_2_439ba232		A dense aura surrounded the place. {w}The air felt quite heavy to breathe, as a thin beam of light appeared to shift and dance.	game/chapter-2.rpy	277	"[what]"
chapter_2_fd997d1b		Nabisin felt sweaty for a moment, staring intently toward the statuette that was attached to the floor.	game/chapter-2.rpy	278	"[what]"
chapter_2_69fec7e7		No one other than Nabisin noticed the atmosphere around them mutating, manifesting some tempest or solar eclipse. {w}The statuette was too far away, just outside his range of vision to notice the small details. {w}But its silhouette was visible, and it changed its pose.	game/chapter-2.rpy	279	"[what]"
chapter_2_f021b0dd		He couldn’t quite understand what pose it was trying to do or what was happening.	game/chapter-2.rpy	280	"[what]"
chapter_2_3f49a51b		His overwhelmed senses were overcome, the last barrier preventing insanity. {w}The ground felt like it was crumbling; he wanted to either vomit or faint.	game/chapter-2.rpy	281	"[what]"
chapter_2_27d1e408		Then just as suddenly, everything subdued, being cut with the Judge’s harsh voice.	game/chapter-2.rpy	282	"[what]"
chapter_2_2fafacf4	"Judge"	“NABISIN! {w}Are you still with us?”	game/chapter-2.rpy	284	"Judge" "[what]"
chapter_2_d4d4e546	n	“Pardon, I may have entered a state of unwellness; my senses were overwhelmed-”	game/chapter-2.rpy	286	n "[what]"
chapter_2_504fba8b	"Judge"	“Silence! {w}Your time is over. Utudug, who is good, may you speak?”	game/chapter-2.rpy	288	"Judge" "[what]"
chapter_2_b6576132		His ill intentions bathed his face with contempt, but he stood loosely. {w}Calmness was his mask, and his calculated, condescending gestures and words spit like a cobra’s venom.	game/chapter-2.rpy	289	"[what]"
chapter_2_59446fc6	u	“Well, I know much about our infancy and time spent at the temples, cares, and I didn’t hold such grudges against you, Nabisin. {w}I remind you, our activities were weak, but you grew sour of me and my comrades. How can one speak up for you when you clearly can’t handle a playful shove?”	game/chapter-2.rpy	293	u "[what]"
chapter_2_303ead2e	u	“Onto the next matter, your liking is evident; you are feminine. {w}Girl-like. {w}Your taste is vile and that of twisted nature. {w}That’s very much why the gods had passed down the laws we know and exercise on this land, which by your own narrative is being punished by divine intervention or lack thereof.”	game/chapter-2.rpy	294	u "[what]"
chapter_2_ab66ebe8	u	“You are practically a female, Nabisin. {w}Accept it. {w}Dress like one of them; your slender physique reminds me of a slave I once had who married a mutt and managed to become free."	game/chapter-2.rpy	295	u "[what]"
chapter_2_9a8369d8	u	"Much to your surprise I’m sure, I’m merciful and have bid them farewell. {w}But if you can’t bear the pains of a man, then fifty blows and becoming a eunuch shall suffice your perverted desires.”	game/chapter-2.rpy	296	u "[what]"
chapter_2_942efd74		Whispers filled the room left and right. {w}People were sure Utudug was right, but they also discussed the possibility of this going too far.	game/chapter-2.rpy	297	"[what]"
chapter_2_a3a10ea1		It’s been three years since the last time someone was beaten and made a eunuch.	game/chapter-2.rpy	298	"[what]"
chapter_2_fb9f90e3		Sure, things change. People become softer or harder over time, but it has come to the attention that, indeed, there were more pressing matters at the moment. {w}Likewise was what Nabisin had brought to the table.	game/chapter-2.rpy	299	"[what]"
chapter_2_4164e453		Men can change the laws to better suit their needs, and the last time this happened, people decided it was too harsh a punishment.	game/chapter-2.rpy	300	"[what]"
chapter_2_e4dd16a5		Nevertheless, Utudug was adamant about his beliefs and spewed his poison everywhere.	game/chapter-2.rpy	301	"[what]"
chapter_2_62a5d026		The judge struggled to reestablish order in the room by speaking up, but his voice refused to reach anyone once the whispers became conversations and conversations became disagreements. But then…	game/chapter-2.rpy	302	"[what]"
chapter_2_0bab1f0c	"Judge"	“ENOUGH!”	game/chapter-2.rpy	304	"Judge" "[what]"
chapter_2_cc5179b4		Everyone went quiet, knowing he had the final word on this case. Each of them resented but complied with the call.	game/chapter-2.rpy	305	"[what]"
chapter_2_bc0858af		Not only was Nabisin’s fate given to others to meddle with, but his temper once again started to become increasingly hard to control once he started to stare at the statuette.	game/chapter-2.rpy	306	"[what]"
