chapter_2_91cd286c		The voice of the judge started to get muffled as the room goes silent.	game/chapter-2.rpy	310	"[what]"
chapter_2_0e125cd8		As the statuette moved, Nabisin stroked another pose mimicking its elusive dance, expecting something, if anything, to happen. {w}He didn’t lose his composure because he knew unless something happened would be soon sentenced to a barbaric punishment that would debilitate him forever.	game/chapter-2.rpy	313	"[what]"
chapter_2_983f13ef		The statuette struck another pose, and Nabisin already knew to follow. {w}Meanwhile, the judge tried to raise his voice once more, and Nabisin ignored him. Locked in a trance-like state, he danced at the statuette’s will as if nothing else mattered.	game/chapter-2.rpy	314	"[what]"
chapter_2_dafb0974		The image he had hoped to see again flashed before his eyes; the palace descended in chaos, the light sources flickered, and gushes of wind intruded with all kinds of scents.	game/chapter-2.rpy	316	"[what]"
chapter_2_a09adfc4		Nabisin didn’t think to connect his dance to the sudden shift in atmosphere. Winds became stronger and stronger, the floor started to shift a little bit, a tempest seemed to form outside, and on cue, it started raining.	game/chapter-2.rpy	318	"[what]"
chapter_2_6de8c901		Finally, the statuette’s dance seemed to reach its eventual end. The symphony of screams, chaotic shuffling, and Utudug bracing himself in terror before being thrown at a wall was probably the best scene Nabisin could imagine, and it was happening right before his eyes.	game/chapter-2.rpy	320	"[what]"
chapter_2_decafed4		Was he doing all of that by following the movements? Was it magic? Some sort of favor of the gods? Or just a coincidence? As he struck the final pose, he didn’t know or seek to question further.	game/chapter-2.rpy	323	"[what]"
chapter_2_beb72bc1		With it, time seemed to return to its natural flow, but something awful was bound to happen.	game/chapter-2.rpy	324	"[what]"
chapter_2_52d21a2b		Ripples through the ground grew steadily; the judge seemed to struggle enough to hold himself upright. Meanwhile, Nabisin barely felt his feet shuffle. He was still waiting for the statuette to act more than create some cracks for his accusors to stumble upon.	game/chapter-2.rpy	325	"[what]"
chapter_2_13ad27e9		Suddenly, with the tremor of an earthquake, the palace crumbled upon itself, brick by brick falling.The structure was barely holding itself, revealing a giant hole that engulfed everyone around Nabisin. The absolute horror on his face was notable, but he felt they earned their judgment.	game/chapter-2.rpy	328	"[what]"
chapter_2_8247b30c		Perhaps not everyone deserved the fate of getting swallowed by the bowels of the Earth, perhaps even the judge, but now the hole was getting bigger and bigger.	game/chapter-2.rpy	329	"[what]"
chapter_2_4b3dc237		He wasn’t sure whether Shelibuum left the room in time; all he knew was that the place had become a husk of itself. {w}And he was standing in an unaffected pillar, a single section that had not crumbled.	game/chapter-2.rpy	330	"[what]"
chapter_2_1208c8e2		There’s no doubt that that was beyond what Nabisin knew. {w}Could he even call that magic? Maybe it was the craft of a god in his favor, but the statue suggested that he himself had done it. 	game/chapter-2.rpy	331	"[what]"
chapter_2_b8319dc7		No matter how much he wanted to believe it was an external factor, he somehow did that, and in the process he killed Utudug, the very man who wanted to see him frail and devoid of life.	game/chapter-2.rpy	332	"[what]"
chapter_2_52c2ce76		By the time the earthquake subsided, Nabisin thought to himself. I guess that’s it, but where do I go from here?	game/chapter-2.rpy	333	"[what]"
chapter_2_71edad13		Quietness overcame the echoing sounds of crumbling bricks and cracks opening. {w}Out of the mud that became the floor, a monster shouted at the top of his lungs. {w}A hand stuck out, and then the muzzle of a gray cat once called Utudug came into view.	game/chapter-2.rpy	334	"[what]"
chapter_2_66c1597f	u	“YOU! GRNNRNNRNANNGNGNNARHA!”	game/chapter-2.rpy	336	u "[what]"
chapter_2_37a07141	u	“You’re going to pay for this, girl-like abomination on the face of the gods. May you die painfully under the rivers-”	game/chapter-2.rpy	337	u "[what]"
chapter_2_367b6576		His distorted face of hatred and vengeance was all that Nabisin could see as Utudug rapidly became snail- like, his legs had been crushed by the earthquake he had summoned.	game/chapter-2.rpy	338	"[what]"
chapter_2_b904a444		Then, it came to Nabisin he needed to do this. {w}He wanted to. {w}As much as kindness and reciprocity was his motif, his anger overwhelmed all other senses.	game/chapter-2.rpy	339	"[what]"
